    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_2",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Garajonay National Park (Spanish: \"Parque nacional de Garajonay\" , ] ) is located in the center and north of the island of La Gomera, one of the Canary Islands (Spain). It was declared a national park in 1981 and a World Heritage Site by UNESCO in 1986. It occupies 40 km (15 sq mi) and it extends into each of the six municipalities on the island.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.9999999764358871,
